# Gapless fast path: THE ARM PATCH. Stacks on top of 0020-0025 and is in
# the framework manifest, so both release images ship the fast path armed.
# It was added after the Phase D observation named in gapless_patch.md
# (resident decoder accepting the stock 0x65 open exchange after
# end-of-stream) was recorded in emulation (patches/harness/milestone2.md).
# The system side now runs in the transition rig (patches/gapless/rig/);
# hardware timing is still unmeasured.
name: gapless-6-arm
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03051676
gate: build refuses unless the 2 bytes at the target equal `expect`
  (the gate cave as installed by 0022); the finished image must also
  pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: One branch inside the gate cave (0022), at cave+0x12. As
  built by 0022 it is an unconditional branch to the stock path (02e0),
  so the gate always runs the full reset-and-start body. This patch makes
  it `bne` (02d1): when core 1 is running and the requested decoder
  module is the retained one, the gate returns without the reload and
  the resident decoder takes the next file's 0x65 open. With 0024 that
  is every natural end-of-track advance between tracks of one format.
expect: 02e0
replace: 02d1
